      "published_utc": "2026-10-22T16:13:17+00:00",
      "summary": "<p>Contern, Luxembourg, October 22nd, 2026, CyberNewswire Gcore is offering its WAAP Enterprise plan free of charge to any government body or public agency until December 31, 2026. The offer follows the php2shell vulnerabilities that forced public websites offline across Europe earlier this week. Gcore WAAP blocks the php2shell attack path (CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619) by default [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://gbhackers.com/gcore-makes-enterprise-security-bundle-free-for-public-agencies-until-end-of-the-year/\">Gcore Makes Enterprise Security Bundle Free for Public Agencies Until End of the Year</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://gbhackers.com\">GBHackers Security | #1 Globally Trusted Cyber Security News Platform</a>.</p>",
